</ul><h1>Fragrant</h1><p>Okay, so let’s just get this out of the way right off the bat.</p>
<p>Yes, these are scented. The scent in question? “Boutique hotel.” Which means they smell like… what? A tiny room with a double bed that costs $357 a night because the lobby has mismatched couches?</p>
<p>Anyway, I know you won’t be happy about this. I too prefer my clothes to come out of the wash smelling like clean fabric and little else.</p>
<p>But maybe you could reserve these for those particularly malodorous loads. Like, for example, exercise clothes.</p>
<p>That’s what Amazon user Jeri Ewing did:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I hit the gym five days a week, and my biggest headache used to be the lingering smell in my moisture-wicking shirts that regular liquid detergent just couldn’t seem to touch. I started using these sheets and the scent is actually strong enough to neutralize that stubborn old gym bag odor without being flowery. I just toss a single sheet into the drum with my leggings and sports bras, and it dissolves completely even on the cold, delicate cycle I use for my high-end athletic wear.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Strong enough to cover up the nastiness, but not flowery. Sounds great, honestly.</p>
